---
title: Price
order: 5
description: Prices, sale prices and "from" prices, formatted with Intl.NumberFormat.
---
{% from "docs.njk" import example, usage, props %}
{% from "components/price/price.njk" import price %}
<header class="docs-header">
  <p class="docs-eyebrow">Component · Partial</p>
  <h1>Price</h1>
  <p class="docs-lede">Quiet and exact. Sales are just a struck-through old price, with no colour. Formats Shopify money in pounds, with no pence on whole amounts (£450, but £45.50). The browser uses the same code in <code>src/scripts/lib/money.js</code> to update the price when someone picks a print size.</p>
</header>

<section class="docs-section" aria-labelledby="use">
  <h2 id="use">Use it</h2>
  {% set code %}{% raw %}{% from "components/price/price.njk" import price %}
{{ price(variant) }}                     {# { price, compareAtPrice } #}
{{ price(product, { size: "lg" }) }}     {# { priceRange, compareAtPriceRange }: shows "From" when prices differ #}{% endraw %}{% endset %}
  {{ usage(code) }}
  {{ props([
    ["input", "Variant | Product", "Straight from the Storefront API."],
    ["size", "\"lg\"", "Bigger, in Lora, for the product page."],
    ["onRequest", "boolean", "Shows “Price on request” instead. Pass product | isPriceOnRequest."]
  ]) }}
</section>

<section class="docs-section" aria-labelledby="variants">
  <h2 id="variants">Variants</h2>
  <div class="docs-examples">
    {% set ex %}{{ price(mock.byHandle["sun-hat-with-tulip"]) }}{% endset %}
    {{ example("Single price (an original)", ex) }}
    {% set ex %}{{ price(mock.byHandle["sun-hat-with-tulip-print"]) }}{% endset %}
    {{ example("From (a print with several sizes)", ex) }}
    {% set ex %}{{ price(mock.byHandle["pink-check-print"].variants.nodes[0]) }}{% endset %}
    {{ example("On sale", ex) }}
    {% set ex %}{{ price(mock.byHandle["sun-hat-with-tulip"], { size: "lg" }) }}{% endset %}
    {{ example("Large", ex) }}
    {% set ex %}{{ price(mock.byHandle["large-interior-redland"], { onRequest: true }) }}{% endset %}
    {{ example("Price on request (tag price-on-request in Shopify)", ex) }}
    {% set ex %}{{ price({ price: { amount: "45.5", currencyCode: "GBP" } }) }}{% endset %}
    {{ example("With pence", ex) }}
  </div>
</section>

<section class="docs-section" aria-labelledby="a11y">
  <h2 id="a11y">Accessibility</h2>
  <ul class="docs-list">
    <li>Sale prices read as “£35, on sale, Was £45”. The struck-through price isn't left to visual styling alone.</li>
  </ul>
</section>
